<title>AUSTRIA: First Austrian 1996 grp net up 8.3 pct.</title>
<headline>First Austrian 1996 grp net up 8.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(figures in millions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>					 1996		  1995</p>
<p> Group operating		  2,243	     up 2.7 pct</p>
<p> Group pre-tax			834	     up 24.9 pct</p>
<p> Group net			    655	     up 8.3 pct</p>
<p> Dividend (schillings)	     16		   16</p>
<p> Group operating revenue	8,797	     down 5.0 pct</p>
<p> Group operating costs	  6,554	     down 7.4 pct</p>
<p> Group total assets (billion)   272	     up 3.3 pct</p>
<p> Parent operating		 1,950	     up 10.9 pct</p>
<p> Parent pre-tax		     741	     up 43.3 pct</p>
<p> Parent net			   602	     up 22.6 pct</p>
<p> Parent operating revenue     6,600	     up 2.6 pct</p>
<p> Parent operating costs	 4,700	     down 0.5 pct</p>
<p> Parent total assets (billion)  225	     up 3.2 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Die Erste Oesterreichische Spar-Casse Bank AG (First Austrian) acquired a majority stake in Austria's GiroCredit Bank in March, creating the nation's second biggest bank.</p>
<p>NOTE - In a statement, First Austrian said parent first quarter operating profit rose almost 30 percent. Operating income was up 5.7 percent and operating costs down 0.9 percent. -- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
</text>
